      "writtenOn": "2021-11-08T17:44:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I wanted to ask about that. This reland (as-is) can\u0027t really land - it regressed performance on a bunch of chrome benchmarks pretty badly. Luckily, it was all on Android devices. The important thing there is that those devices have NEON, and the implementation of div255 on NEON is actually correct, vs. the approximation used on other architectures.\n\nSo, I could make the force_highp thing conditional on NEON (but that\u0027s ugly, and only fixes the precision problem in this one code path), or... we could try to make div255 accurate on all platforms. How bad would it be for performance if we changed div255 from:\n\n  return (v+255)/256;\n  \nto:\n\n  v +\u003d 128;\n  return (v+(v/256))/256;\n  \n... knowing that it\u0027s used throughout the lowp blending stages, etc?",
      "parentUuid": "adc1395a_20d18452",
      "revId": "d2bf54ec001fd87240c110583e91686cb927a304",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b116bd36_84e9e345",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-08T19:16:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that div255() is the wrong abstraction. I think we want is\nU16 premul(c, a) {\n  U16 t \u003d c * a + 0x80\n  return (t + (t \u003e\u003e 8)) \u003e\u003e 8;\n}\n\n\nI think the real question is \"how often do we have to premul?\"",
      "parentUuid": "68fd7423_c0308c14",
      "revId": "d2bf54ec001fd87240c110583e91686cb927a304",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39cb0426_a8d17a44",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-08T19:33:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From a quick scan of the code, premul doesn\u0027t appear to happen *too* often:\n- Sprite blitter does it to a known (paint) color, which is totally unnecessary.\n- Various color filters do it (after converting to unpremul and doing some work, to get back to premul output)\n- Gradients do it depending on the flag (interpolate in premul or not)\n- And SkColorSpaceXformSteps does it, which is used in a few places (GrConvertPixels, SkConvertPixels, more color filters, etc...)\n\nSo, not that often overall. We could make opt to make premul use the more accurate rounding, and leave div255 separate. But does that make sense? My first reaction was no - if we have a better result, let\u0027s use it all the time. But all of the other situations aren\u0027t as sensitive to precision. They\u0027re blending or filtering results, which are strictly a one-way operation. The premul thing is much more sensitive, because of the unpremul -\u003e premul round-trip issue. So I can be convinced that only doing the better rounding for lowp premul is valid. Let me put that together (it should also avoid the huge number of GM diffs from PS3).",
      "parentUuid": "b116bd36_84e9e345",
      "revId": "d2bf54ec001fd87240c110583e91686cb927a304",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
